			<div class="content" id="post-content-1373466">
									

<p>Make that a second big problem. It seems like it would have no forms of propulsion in space, but to return every ~76 years, it would have to do about <em>10% light speed</em> to go to and from the nearest star in that timescale.<br />
Even travelling at <em>c</em>, that still limits is to only a handful of the closest stars.</p>
<p>I do still like the idea of it, but you're going to have to either up the velocity or give it a much longer timescale between leaving and returning.<br />
Upping the velocity gives time dilation on it, too, which means it would live longer, so it would get more travel cycles in it's life.</p>

